  "observations": [
    "The two new 1688x780 originals were inspected directly. Pause shows the ordinary DEV14 RETURN TO MINE menu without the hero; state has zero active rigs.",
    "dev14-resumed.png shows the complete Worn character facing forward near raster x580-648,y468-575, lower on the Surface path than its start. No visible viewport cut, duplicate body, missing limb or material regression.",
    "The resume-real-input state moves from [600,650] to [600,689.666809082031], a 39.6668-unit displacement. Subsequent captured samples retain that position, mining=false, menu=false, gear=worn, pickaxe=1, drill=0 and one native rig; updates increase 87 to 99. This closes the previously open post-resume input gate.",
    "Prior unobscured captures establish the approved Worn appearance, eight directional mining cases, held/rush release, iron/Burrower fallback, red outfit reentry, Surface/Rootwound/Hub visibility and pause release. Hub pixels and state corroborate the cache fix.",
    "Final and prior consoles contain no runtime error lines. Damage and input conclusions use the recorded state and observer checks, not still-derived motion inference."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "V1",
      "severity": "coverage_caveat",
      "finding": "The Deepheart command captures its restored Hub destination, not the separate Deepheart cavern.",
